<<<
4. Fly-leaf is a blank leaf forming part of something printed, especially one between the cover & the titlepage of a book, or at the end of a circular or leaflet; it is not another name for a leaflet, which is, however, sometimes called a fly-sheet.
===
**4.** *Fly-leaf* is a blank leaf forming part of something printed, especially one between the cover & the title-page of a book, or at the end of a circular or leaflet; it is not another name for a leaflet, which is, however, sometimes called a *fly-sheet.*
>>>

